   "markingNotes": "Example answer: Both kingdoms are eukaryotic and have cell walls, but fungal walls are made of chitin and plant walls of cellulose. Fungi are heterotrophs that digest food outside their hyphae and absorb it, whereas plants are autotrophs that photosynthesise using chloroplasts. Fungi store glycogen; plants store starch. Fungi are built of hyphae and reproduce by spores, whereas most plants have roots, stems and leaves."
