      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p2",
      "description": "Its members are very diverse (photosynthetic algae, animal-like protozoa, fungus-like forms)",
      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p3",
      "description": "Molecular (DNA/rRNA) evidence shows they are not all closely related / do not share one recent common ancestor, so the group does not reflect evolutionary relationships",
      "marks": 1
     }
    ]
   },
   "markingNotes": "Example answer: Protoctista is defined by what its members are not: eukaryotes that do not fit the fungi, plants or animals. Its members are very diverse, from seaweeds to *Amoeba* and *Plasmodium*, and DNA evidence shows that they are not all closely related, so the kingdom does not reflect evolutionary relationships. Splitting it would group organisms by common ancestry."
